ONE HONEST QUALIFICATION on the performance clause: the assertion is made against
cost-report's PREDICATES, not against an absent workflow.performance event, because
the cost-report Lambda is not in this harness. The test says so itself (:1023-1028).
That is the right call for a unit replay, but it means no single test proves the
end-to-end "no event was published" — that link rests on cost-report's own
index.test.mjs, and on the KNOWN CONSEQUENCE its source documents at index.mjs:531-534
("anything counting runs by workflow.performance rows under-counts no-op sweeps, by
design").

UNDER THE SHIPPED DEFAULT (shadow) THE FULL CHAIN STILL RUNS -- this is the answer
to the asked question, and it is asserted, not inferred:
  - one sweep.detection_observed with wouldClose:true (so the intent is recorded),
  - terminalClaims for nothing-to-remove == [] and no PR label written,
  - orchestrator.unblocked == [REVIEW, QA, CI] with unblockedBy == DETECT,
  - countOfType('workflow.complete') === 1,
  - and each of the reviewer/QA/CI personas dispatched exactly once (:894).
So on a default deploy c2uqki's four wasted personas are still spent. D2 only
observes. That is the documented design, but it means the acceptance item's
headline behaviour is off by default.

